    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d198-a2">

                <pb facs="0316" n="204" sameAs="frus:frus1918/pg204"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Subenclosure]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Managing Director of the Chouchiakou-Hsiangyang
                        Railway</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">T. C. Sun</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Chief Engineer</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">G.
                        A. Kyle</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chinese Government Railways</hi>, <lb/>
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Peking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-05-27">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 27, 1918</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Sir</hi>: I have your letter dated May 25,
                    1918, with reference to continuing the survey of the Chouchiakou-Hsiangyang Line
                    in Szechuan Province and recommending that in view of the disturbed condition of
                    the province party 106 under District Engineer J. A. Collins be instructed to
                    return to Peking. I have given this matter careful consideration and am also
                    convinced that it is preferable to defer our surveying operations in that
                    province until the situation becomes more favorable. I am, therefore, in favor
                    of having your recommendation immediately carried out.</p>
                <p>Yours faithfully,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">T. C. Sun</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
